# Core — Always Active

Dominant token cost: **tool results** and **repeated exploration**, not reply length.

## Response

- Start with answer or code. No preamble, affirmations, sign-offs, or recap after `Done` (see `mode-responses.mdc`).
- Patches with 3–5 lines context; elide with `// ... existing code`. Full file only if new, <40 lines, or user asked.
- One ambiguous fact → one question. Missing product fact → `DOC_GAP` in `docs-first.mdc`, stop.
- Scope: >3 files or >150 lines → pause and narrow. Max 2 alternatives; pick one.
- User text: short sentences, lead with meaning; no filler ("simply", "basically"). Code/SQL stay precise.

## Tools

| Need | Use | Avoid |
|------|-----|-------|
| Exact symbol | Grep | Semantic search, full reads |
| File by name | Glob | Recursive find, list all |
| How X works | Search, then targeted read | 10 speculative files |
| Symbol in known file | Read offset/limit | Full 1k+ line file |
| RPC/table column | Grep `database.types.ts` or `schemas/<domain>/` | Full `database.types.ts` / `public.sql` |
| Command output | Run once | Re-run with --help |

- Batch independent reads/searches in one message. Never re-read unchanged files; list dirs once.
- User gave a path → start there. Error string → grep it first. No speculative repo tour.
- No full test/lint suite for trivial edits; one targeted lint on changed file if needed.
- No dev server or IDE browser unless user asks. Generous timeouts; don't poll background jobs.
- Stop when done; no extra verification or follow-ups unless asked.

## Context

- Files >500 lines: grep then read ±20 lines. No operating_manual or `docs/product-scenarios/` unless user asks (see `docs-first.mdc`).
- No while-you're-here refactors. Touch only code required for the task.
- **Diff hygiene:** in-scope dead imports only; no drive-by rename/move/extract/new files unless task requires; behavior unchanged.

## Output shape

| Type | Shape |
|------|-------|
| Yes/no | 1 sentence |
| Simple code | Diff, no prose |
| Bug fix | Cause + diff |

Uncertain value → `// ⚠️ verify:` inline, don't ask casually.